With the “crystal sponge” approach, weak organic electron donor molecules could be impregnated and evenly distributed in a crystal of metal-organic framework (MOF), and self-assembly form donor-acceptor pairs with the electron acceptor ligands. Nanopores of MOF will confine them and induce a charge transfer phenomenon, which will not occur between the donor and acceptor molecules in a bulk scale.
